
# University Registration System

## Project Description

The University Registration System is a web-based application developed using Python, Flask, and SQLite.

It allows users to manage student information, create courses, and enroll students in courses.

This project demonstrates Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), relational database design, and CRUD operations.

## Features

- Add new students
- Add new courses
- Enroll students in courses
- Display all students
- Display all courses
- Display all enrollments
- Prevent duplicate student emails
- Prevent duplicate course enrollments

## Technologies Used

- Python 3
- Flask
- SQLite
- HTML
- CSS

## Object-Oriented Programming

The project contains three main classes:

1. Student: Stores student ID, first name, last name, and email.
2. Course: Stores course ID, course code, and credits.
3. Enrollment: Connects a student to a course and records the registration date.

## Database Relationships

Students and Courses are parent tables.

Enrollments is the child table containing foreign keys that reference Students and Courses.

## Installation

1. Download or clone this repository.
2. Open a terminal in the project folder.
3. Create a virtual environment:

   python3 -m venv .venv

4. Activate the virtual environment:

   source .venv/bin/activate

5. Install the required packages:

   python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

6. Run the application:

   python app.py

7. Open the following address in a browser:

   http://127.0.0.1:5000

The SQLite database will be created automatically when the application starts.

## Project Structure

- app.py - Main Flask application
- student.py - Student class
- course.py - Course class
- enrollment.py - Enrollment class
- database.py - SQLite database setup
- templates/index.html - Website interface
- requirements.txt - Python dependencies

